      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to translate the given statement into a mathematical inequality and then solve it step by step.\n\nThe statement says: \"The difference when the product of 4 and a number is subtracted from 16 is greater than 10.\"\n\nLet's denote the number by \\( x \\). The product of 4 and \\( x \\) is \\( 4x \\). The statement can be rewritten as:\n\\[ 16 - 4x > 10 \\]\n\nNext, we need to isolate \\( x \\). We start by subtracting 16 from both sides of the inequality:\n\\[ -4x > 10 - 16 \\]\n\\[ -4x > -6 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we divide both sides by -4. Remember that dividing by a negative number reverses the inequality sign:\n\\[ x < \\frac{-6}{-4} \\]\n\\[ x < \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\\[ x < 1.5 \\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) must be a positive integer, we look at the positive integers less than 1.5. The only positive integer that satisfies this condition is \\( x = 1 \\).\n\nTo verify, we substitute \\( x = 1 \\) back into the original problem:\n\\[ 16 - 4 \\cdot 1 > 10 \\]\n\\[ 16 - 4 = 12 \\]\n\\[ 12 > 10 \\]\n\nThe inequality holds true, so \\( x = 1 \\) is a solution. There are no other positive integers less than 1.5.\n\nTherefore, the number of positive integers that satisfy the given conditions is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
